      "number": 265,
      "shortId": "8FSPU",
      "priority": 1,
      "shortName": "notify-blocked-keybinding",
      "title": "notify-blocked-keybinding: Notification when an action is blocked by policy",
      "status": "planned",
      "description": "Show a toast notification when a user-triggered action is blocked by the interaction policy (FocusDomain::Floating blocking TiledOnly/WorkspaceLevel/AlwaysAllowed actions, or any other RouteDecision::Block).\n\nPREREQUISITE (shared with the config-reload task): wire a toast host in the app — the `heca-grid-ui` `Toast`/`ToastStack` widgets exist (`heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/toast.rs`, `toast_stack.rs`) but NO host is mounted today (`grep ToastStack heca/src/` = empty). Mount a `ToastStack` as a retained overlay band (or chrome region) and expose a `push_toast`/notification API reachable from the interaction dispatch path. Keep it minimal and reusable (the full Notification System feature fc19894f owns the richer store/lifecycle/routing — do not duplicate that).\n\nHOOK: in `heca/src/app/interaction.rs`, the policy block happens in `route_action` (~:471) returning `RouteDecision::Block` (arms at :427/:435/:443/:450/:458 + floating-domain blocks :491/:501/:508). The blocked action is silently discarded at the `dispatch_action`/`dispatch_intent` chokepoints (AGENTS: \"silently discarded — debug log\"). Fire the toast there with the blocked action's user-facing label (resolve via `ActionCatalog::label`) — e.g. \"Float toggle blocked (floating pane active)\" or a generic \"Action blocked by policy\". Must be reachable from keyboard + mouse + RPC sources (the block already spans all sources). No hardcoded text — use the ActionCatalog label + a configurable template if needed.\n\nVerify: cargo test + clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features clean; manual check (open a floating pane, press a TiledOnly binding like prefix+Enter/split → toast appears).",
      "notes": "",
