    {
      "id": "eb1cd685-873e-4ed5-a047-8a92b147e211",
      "phaseId": "dcf9ff70-cf6e-416e-8e46-8cc36b4ec233",
      "number": 266,
      "shortId": "5B9X6",
      "priority": 2,
      "shortName": "notify-config-reload",
      "title": "notify-config-reload: Success/warning notification on config reload outcome",
      "status": "planned",
      "description": "Show a toast notification on config reload (`prefix+Shift+r` / `WmAction::ReloadConfig`): a SUCCESS toast when the reload applied the new config, a WARNING toast when the reload failed (bad config.toml) so the user knows the working config was kept and what to fix.\n\nPREREQUISITE (shared with the blocked-keybinding task): wire a toast host in the app — `heca-grid-ui` `Toast`/`ToastStack` exist but no host is mounted today. Same host as the blocked-keybinding task; build it once.\n\nHOOK: `heca/src/main.rs:96` `HecaApp::reload_config` — today the error arm only `eprintln!(\"[heca] reload failed: {e}\")` (:101) and `eprintln!(\"[heca] fix config.toml and press prefix+Shift+r to retry\")`; the success arm has no user feedback at all (silent). Replace/augment the `eprintln!` with a warning toast (including the error message) on failure, and add a success toast (\"Config reloaded\") on the success path. `heca/src/handlers.rs:2312` `handle_reload_config` sets `pending_reload = true`; the actual reload runs in `main.rs::reload_config` (called from :240). The toast API must be reachable from `main.rs` (push via `event_proxy` or a state field).\n\nNo hardcoded text where a config/template can live — keep the toast messages in one place, configurable if practical. Must be reachable from keyboard (the ReloadConfig binding) and RPC.\n\nVerify: cargo test + clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features clean; manual check (good config → success toast on prefix+Shift+r; bad config → warning toast with the error, working config preserved).",
      "notes": "",
